    <listOfParameters>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="f_renal_function" name="renal function" value="1" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <blockquote>
              <p>1.0: increased kidney function
1.0: normal kidney function (healthy control)
&lt;1.0: decreased kidney function</p>
            </blockquote>
            <p>Renal function relative to the healthy glomerular filtration rate
GFR_base, which is 101 ml/min at 75 kg; a measured creatinine
clearance of X ml/min is the renal function X/101.</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="GFR_base" name="glomerular filtration rate (healthy)" value="101" units="ml_per_min" constant="true"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000009" id="OMEOHEX_f" name="renal clearance of 5-hydroxyomeprazole relative to the GFR" value="1.83915259344785" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>The renal clearance of 5-hydroxyomeprazole is OMEOHEX_f times the GFR:
above 1 a net secretion. The 5-hydroxyomeprazole of the plasma is
excreted in the urine (13.5 % of the dose in extensive metabolizers
[Sohn1992]), half-life about 1 hr [Andersson1990a].</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
